### The Code, Step by Step

Let us see how we tell the computer to show a message on screen:

```cpp
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;

int main() {
    cout << "Hello, world!" << "\n";
    cout << "This is my first program." << "\n";
    return 0;
}
```

**What each line does:**
- `#include <iostream>` -- tells the computer 'I need the tools to display text on screen'
- `using namespace std;` -- a shortcut so we do not have to write extra code every time
- `int main() { }` -- the main box where all your important code lives
- `cout << "Hello!" << "\n";` -- pushes text to the screen; `"\n"` presses ENTER automatically
- `return 0;` -- announces that everything went fine

**Rule to remember:** If you forget `;` at the end of a line, the compiler stops and you get an error. Always put `;` and you will be fine.

